{"id": "EUVD-2026-91458", "enisaUuid": "7af94064-9f0c-37a0-9dbe-00582b022e89", "description": "YesWiki before 4.6.7 contains a cross-site request forgery vulnerability in the autoupdate UpdateAction that allows attackers to delete installed packages via unprotected GET requests. Attackers can lure a logged-in administrator to a crafted link with action=delete and a package parameter to remove extensions like bazar, breaking core site functionality.", "datePublished": "2026-10-02T11:38:20", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-02T13:33:43", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:L/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/YesWiki/yeswiki/security/advisories/GHSA-jp5c-grgj-624x", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/yeswiki-before-4.6.7-csrf-package-deletion-via-autoupdate-updateaction"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-104447", "GHSA-g4cv-jj47-pfj7"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "455ca9ba-ed69-3376-b0a3-0ab57e81974f", "product": {"name": "yeswiki", "vendor": {"name": "YesWiki"}}, "product_version": "0 <4.6.7"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "dda95a20-d5dd-3d72-b5e3-9b5cafec458a", "vendor": {"name": "YesWiki"}}], "isExploited": false}